  notes: "iOS defaults (unit: pt = 1/163 inch).\n\nSOURCE: UIKit UILongPressGestureRecognizer
    defaults for touchSlopDp (allowableMovement 10 pt) and longPressTimeoutMs (minimumPressDuration
    0.5 s).\n\nNO OS VALUES are read on iOS yet: UIKit does not expose its gesture
    thresholds. Density comes from Screen.dpi, then fallbackDpi (no native plugin
    for now).\n\nGUESSES - iOS does not publish these, so Android's values are used
    as-is (1 pt is roughly 1 dp). Check on a real iPhone (plan.md Q2):\n- fallbackDpi
    460: typical modern iPhone.\n- doubleTapTimeoutMs 300, doubleTapMinTimeMs 40, doubleTapSlopDp
    100.\n- multiFingerTapWindowMs 150.\n- minFlingVelocityDps 50, maxFlingVelocityDps
    8000, velocityWindowMs 100.\n- swipeAngleToleranceDeg 30, minRotationDeg 5.\n-
    minScalingSpanDp 170, edgeSlopDp 12."
